---
// Lesson 11.2b — Create PT: Submit as Final
// hybrid CPT: Digital Portfolio submission; final checklist; celebration.
import Lesson from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';

const body = `<h1>11.2b — Create PT: Submit as Final</h1>

<p class="lesson-lead">
    Today the Create PT becomes COLLEGE BOARD PROPERTY. You will
    open the Digital Portfolio, upload the program, the video, and
    the PPR, and press the button your teacher cannot press for
    you. Then — a unit's worth of weight off — we pivot to the
    exam itself.
</p>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity hybrid">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Submission</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~35 min</span>
    </div>

    <p><strong>What goes in the Digital Portfolio (three things,
    in order):</strong></p>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>Program code (the .zip or the single file):</strong>
            your whole project — including the lines your PPR
            cites, verbatim</li>
        <li><strong>Video:</strong> your sub-60s one take
            (<a href="11.2a.html">11.2a</a>)</li>
        <li><strong>PPR:</strong> uploaded as your exam-day
            reference</li>
    </ol>
    <p><strong>That is the whole April submission.</strong> The four
    written responses are <em>not</em> part of it — you write those in
    Bluebook on May 14, with your PPR open. The drafts you wrote in
    <a href="11.1e.html">11.1e</a> are your notes for that day, not a
    Portfolio upload.</p>

    <p><strong>The final final check — read aloud with a
    partner:</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>Every code excerpt in the PPR exists verbatim in the
            submitted program</li>
        <li>Video plays from the Portfolio preview (not just your
            disk)</li>
        <li>No names, no school, no faces without permission
            forms</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Then <strong>Submit as Final.</strong> The deadline is
    April 30, 11:59 PM ET — you are submitting EARLY, because
    upload failures happen and the Portfolio does not care whose
    fault. Take the confirmation screenshot (yes, really) and put
    it in your repo: <code>commit "11.2b: SUBMITTED"</code>.</p>

</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity hybrid">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Pivot</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~15 min</span>
    </div>

    <p><strong>The exam is next.</strong> Your Create PT is in — and
    it shares that 30% of your score with the four written-response
    prompts you will answer about it on exam day. The other 70% rests
    on the multiple-choice section alone. Both happen May 14, 8:00 AM,
    Session 1, in Bluebook: 70 multiple-choice questions (120
    minutes), then 4 written responses (60 minutes) — WR1/WR2 on the
    END-OF-COURSE exam are the real thing, and your
    <a href="11.1e.html">11.1e</a> drafts were rehearsal for exactly
    these; your PPR is open for all four. Everything from
    <a href="9.1.html">9.1</a> to here is now MC practice
    material.</p>


    <div class="checklist">
        <h3>Checkpoint — before moving on, you must be able to:</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>See the Portfolio confirmation (screenshot in repo)</li>
            <li>Verify the three uploaded artifacts match the final
                code, the final video, and the final PPR</li>
            <li>State what is done: the Create PT is submitted —
                part of the 30% block, banked</li>
            <li>State what remains: May 14, 8 AM, Bluebook — the
                70% MCQ section, plus the 4 written responses that
                share that same 30% block</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <p>Need a deeper explanation? These pages cover the same concepts:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../exam/index.html">Exam Hub</a> — dates, format, everything</li>
        <li><a href="../exam/written-responses.html">Written Responses</a> — the four prompts you answer May 14</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Next: <a href="11.3.html">11.3 — Written-Response Practice (PPR in hand)</a></p>
</div>`;
---
<Lesson id="11.2b" title="11.2b Create PT: Submit as Final — AP CS Principles" root=".." css="../style.css">
  <Fragment set:html={body} />
</Lesson>
